{"type":"https://developers.cloudflare.com/support/troubleshooting/http-status-codes/cloudflare-5xx-errors/error-525/","title":"Error 525: SSL handshake failed","status":525,"detail":"The SSL/TLS handshake between Cloudflare and the origin server failed. The origin's SSL configuration is not compatible with Cloudflare, possibly due to missing shared cipher suites or an unsupported TLS version.","instance":"a51302707dad95e5","error_code":525,"error_name":"ssl_handshake_failed","error_category":"ssl","ray_id":"a51302707dad95e5","timestamp":"2026-10-27T16:17:12Z","zone":"cf-525.wpmtcf.co","cloudflare_error":true,"retryable":false,"owner_action_required":true,"what_you_should_do":"**Do not retry.** Retrying will not resolve this error. The website operator must fix the origin SSL/TLS configuration. Start by verifying a valid SSL certificate is installed on the origin; if none exists, a free Cloudflare Origin CA certificate (https://developers.cloudflare.com/ssl/origin-configuration/origin-ca/) can be installed as a self-service fix. Other causes include a closed port 443, missing SNI support, or cipher suites incompatible with Cloudflare.","footer":"This error was generated by Cloudflare on behalf of the website owner."}
